This project is a Python program built using Pandas to clean a CSV file containing geographic coordinates (Latitude and Longitude). The script reads the Coordinates.csv file, removes empty rows, validates coordinate values (Latitude must be between -90 to 90 and Longitude must be between -180 to 180), filters out invalid coordinate entries, removes duplicate locations, and finally exports the cleaned dataset as Cleaned_Coordinates.csv. This project is useful for understanding how real-world GIS datasets often contain missing, incorrect, and duplicate values, and how Python can be used to automate the cleaning process efficiently. Note: The coordinates used in this dataset are for reference purposes only and may not be fully accurate.
